{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.DeltaLambdaBindingAssembly","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.DeltaLambdaBindingAssembly","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ArgUPhaseBranchSelection"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DeltaLambdaBindingAssembly.real_substrate_phase_frozen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DeltaLambdaBindingAssembly.real_substrate_phase_frozen","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DeltaLambdaBindingAssembly.lean#L94-L106","doc":"**The real substrate freezes the phase (the wall).** For any substrate\n`q₀ ≥ 1`, the complex argument of `2·ln q₀` is zero — the meridian holonomy\nstays on the real ray. This is the proved fact that the real substrate\nCANNOT source the angular deformation ϑ_K.\n\nCombined with `sign_flip_forces_both_regimes`: the sign flip proves ϑ_K ≠ 0\nat the proton anchor, yet the real substrate gives ϑ = 0. Therefore the source\nof ϑ_K is EXTERNAL to the real substrate — it is the G3 monodromy/Stokes\ndatum (bean `qou-qnnq`). This is not a sorry; it is an honest identification\nof the surviving open input. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DeltaLambdaBindingAssembly.sign_flip_forces_both_regimes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DeltaLambdaBindingAssembly.sign_flip_forces_both_regimes","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DeltaLambdaBindingAssembly.lean#L84-L92","doc":"**The sign flip forces both regimes.** If the binding formula gives a\npositive value at one deformation and a negative value at another (with\nthe same positive `A`), then one deformation is boost-dominated and the\nother is spin-dominated — i.e. `𝔲₁.im² < 𝔲₁.re²` AND `𝔲₂.re² < 𝔲₂.im²`.\nThe angular deformation ϑ_K MUST cross the diagonal between the two anchors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DeltaLambdaBindingAssembly.binding_sign_neg_of_spin_dominated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DeltaLambdaBindingAssembly.binding_sign_neg_of_spin_dominated","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DeltaLambdaBindingAssembly.lean#L78-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DeltaLambdaBindingAssembly.binding_sign_pos_of_boost_dominated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DeltaLambdaBindingAssembly.binding_sign_pos_of_boost_dominated","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DeltaLambdaBindingAssembly.lean#L65-L76","doc":"**Sign from the angular deformation.** If the Stokes constant is positive\n(`A > 0`, physically: GGM gives `A_ω = 3 > 0` for 4₁), then the sign of\n`A · Im 𝔙₄₁(𝔲)` is determined by whether `|Re 𝔲| > |Im 𝔲|` (positive,\nboost-dominated) or `|Re 𝔲| < |Im 𝔲|` (negative, spin-dominated).\n\nIn the `ϑ_K` notation: `S > 0 ↔ ϑ_K² < ln²q₀` (muon-type anchor),\n`S < 0 ↔ ϑ_K² > ln²q₀` (proton-type anchor). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DeltaLambdaBindingAssembly.binding_formula_of_imV₄₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DeltaLambdaBindingAssembly.binding_formula_of_imV₄₁","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DeltaLambdaBindingAssembly.lean#L54-L63","doc":"**The binding formula: imaginary part of A·𝔙₄₁(𝔲).**\nFor any Stokes constant `A` and complex deformation `𝔲 = Re 𝔲 + i·Im 𝔲`,\nthe imaginary part of `A·𝔙₄₁(𝔲)` is `A·κ·(Re²𝔲 − Im²𝔲)`.\n\nThis is the sorry-free composition: `imV₄₁` gives the inner formula,\nscalar multiplication pulls `A` through. The physical content is in\n`imV₄₁` (the figure-eight cusp modulus), not in this assembly step. ","signatureChunk":0}]}